The rules to move from Lojban to predicate logic notation are actually
quite simple if you ignore the "full bridi scope" nonsense: You
convert afterthought connectives to forethought and then you just
start from left to right and move things to the prenex:

su'o da poi prenu cu ricfu gi'e na gleki
=3D su'o da poi prenu ge ricfu gi na gleki
=3D su'o da poi prenu zo'u da ge ricfu gi na gleki
=3D su'o da poi prenu zo'u ge da ricfu gi da na gleki
=3D su'o da poi prenu zo'u ge da ricfu gi naku zo'u da gleki
=3D Ex:R(x)^~G(x)

Notice that in the last step you could say that "na" has "full bridi
scope", but that's only after you have moved all preceding connectives
and quantifiers out of the way, not before.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

